        "root_concepts": "[logic]",
        "section": "philosophy",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "01 - Logic",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "TRUTH-FUNCTIONAL CONNECTIVES:\n  ¬ (negation): ¬T = F, ¬F = T\n  ∧ (conjunction): T only when both true\n  ∨ (disjunction): F only when both false (inclusive or)\n  → (material conditional): F only when antecedent T and consequent F\n    Controversy: \"if p then q\" is true when p is false — vacuous truth\n    \"If the moon is cheese, then 2+2=5\" is TRUE (vacuously)\n    This is not how \"if...then\" works in natural language; logic idealizes it\n  ↔ (biconditional): T when both have same truth value"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-LOGIC.md#010",
      "path": [
        "01-LOGIC.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:philosophy:01-logic, git-history:philosophy:01-logic]",
        "canonical_path": "philosophy/01-LOGIC.md",
        "concepts": "[logic]",
        "current_path": "philosophy/01-LOGIC.md",
        "id": "maxim:philosophy:logic",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "philosophy",
        "remap_from": "[]",
