        "root_concepts": "[logic]",
        "section": "philosophy",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "01 - Logic",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "NORMAL FORMS:\n  CNF (conjunctive normal form): conjunction of clauses (each clause = disjunction of literals)\n    (p ∨ q) ∧ (¬p ∨ r) ∧ (q ∨ ¬r)\n    Key for SAT solvers (DPLL, CDCL)\n  DNF (disjunctive normal form): disjunction of conjunctions\n  Every WFF equivalent to CNF and DNF\n  3-SAT: satisfiability of CNF with exactly 3 literals per clause — NP-complete (Cook-Levin)\n```"
    },
