        "section": "philosophy",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "01 - Logic",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nHILBERT SYSTEM: axiom schemas + modus ponens\n  Axiom schemas (e.g., Łukasiewicz):\n    H1: p → (q → p)\n    H2: (p → (q → r)) → ((p → q) → (p → r))\n    H3: (¬q → ¬p) → (p → q)  [or similar for classical logic]\n  Modus ponens: from φ and φ → ψ, infer ψ\n  Proofs are long but theoretically clean; only one inference rule"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-LOGIC.md#014",
      "path": [
        "01-LOGIC.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:philosophy:01-logic, git-history:philosophy:01-logic]",
