        "module": "philosophy",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[logic]",
        "section": "philosophy",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "01 - Logic",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "NATURAL DEDUCTION (Gentzen/Prawitz):\n  Introduction and elimination rules for each connective\n  ∧I: from φ, ψ, conclude φ ∧ ψ\n  ∧E: from φ ∧ ψ, conclude φ (or ψ)\n  →I: from assuming φ and deriving ψ, conclude φ → ψ (discharge assumption)\n  →E: from φ → ψ and φ, conclude ψ (modus ponens)\n  ¬E: from φ and ¬φ, conclude ψ (ex falso quodlibet — explosion)\n  Classical logic adds: ¬¬E (double negation elimination) or excluded middle (φ ∨ ¬φ)\n  INTUITIONISTIC logic omits ¬¬E / excluded middle (see §3)\n  Curry-Howard: ND proofs ↔ simply typed lambda calculus terms (proof = program)"
    },
